          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:  \nThe patient has genetic generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at 6 years of age. The reported seizure frequency is approximately 6 seizures per week. Genetic etiology is attributed to a pathogenic PCDH19 variant, c.918G>A. The epilepsy is classified as drug responsive. Brain MRI demonstrates nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nCurrent Medication:  \n- Oxcarbazepine, current antiseizure medication\n\nSeizure Burden Summary:  \nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occurring approximately 6 times per week.\n\nAssessment:  \nGenetic generalized epilepsy due to PCDH19 c.918G>A, with generalized tonic-clonic seizures and drug-responsive status. MRI shows nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nPlan:  \n- Continue oxcarbazepine.\n- Continue monitoring seizure frequency and treatment response.",
